Heading path: Modelable Language Reference > 6. Registry Federation and Imports > 6.4 Consumer Entry (Written by the CLI)

The compiler writes a small MDL file back to each upstream peer's `consumers/` directory during the write-back phase. This file is never authored by hand.

```mdl
// consumers/analytics-registry/CustomerOrderSummary@1.mdl
consumer {
  registry:   "analytics-registry"
  projection: "analytics.CustomerOrderSummary@1"
  uses: [
    "customer.Customer@3#a3f8b2c1d4e5f6a7"
  ]
  registeredAt: "2026-05-14T09:05:00Z"
}
```

Heading path: Modelable Playground Architecture > 7.3 RPC protocol

Use a versioned request-response protocol.

```ts
interface RpcRequest<T> {
  protocolVersion: 1;
  id: string;
  method: string;
  payload: T;
}

interface RpcSuccess<T> {
  protocolVersion: 1;
  id: string;
  ok: true;
  result: T;
}

interface RpcFailure {
  protocolVersion: 1;
  id: string;
  ok: false;
  error: {
    code: string;
    message: string;
    details?: unknown;
  };
}
```

